= Notes and citations <notes-and-citations>

A regular note#footnote[An ordinary footnote with _emphasis_.]<writer-fn-ordinary> precedes a note citation @doe2020.

A second note citation @knuth1984[p. 12].

The ordinary note is repeated#footnote(<writer-fn-ordinary>);.

A parent note contains another citation#footnote[Parent note text with a nested note citation @lee2019.]<writer-fn-parent>.

A grouped note citation @doe2020 @lee2019.

Prose in a note style #cite(<doe2020>, form: "prose") retains the engine\'s output.

Hidden #cite(<lee2019>, form: none) adds no note.

